<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates continue to rise.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates continue to rise.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) continued to rise on Monday after the Central Bank's 0.25 percentage-point increase in its overnight borrowing rate last Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks are anticipating a further increase in T-bill rates,&quot; a foreign bank dealer said. The regular weekly auction of Treasury bills will be held later today.</p>
<p>The Central Bank adjusted its rate upward in line with the domestic trend and to support the local currency which had been under attack.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  APRIL 28		 APRIL 25</p>
<p>    1 W		9  7/8		  9 13/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9 13/16		 9  3/4</p>
<p>    1 M		9  7/8		  9 13/16</p>
<p>    2 M		9 15/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10			9 15/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/4		 10  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  9/16		10  1/2</p>
<p>    VAL		29-Apr		  28-Apr</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (63 2) 841-8937</p>
